e happened  onlookers called 9-1-1 as good  samaritans administered cpr to the  40-year-old father of three who they  dragged out of the water witnesses say  it took at least 30 minutes for an  ambulance just to show up they're not  emergency officials they're just two  drivers basically that's what they are  so this is essentially like a taxi yep  it's basically a taxi that says  ambulance  wow  do you feel like they did anything to  try and save your husband's life no it  was just easy  easy i know it's it's another another  person for them  it was it was just easy  sorry that's all you could do  sharogia's husband died  tomorrow you are going to hear more from  her and you're going to meet two of the  good samaritans who tried to save her  husband's life you will also hear  directly from one of the ambulance  drivers who arrived on the scene that  day  and what happened when he got there what  did he actually do  we'll tell you  this is so upsetting david because i  think when you go on vacation just  you almost let your guard down you  certainly don't think that you're going  to die on vacation and certainly not  snorkeling  you think if it does somebody will be  there to help you take it for granted  you're going to call for help and they  come right that's what's going up in the  states wait until you hear tomorrow when  i say to the guy the paramedic yeah when  the states were used to this wait until  you see his reaction but i want you to  know that the good people of nate you  asked how many people lived there  roughly 1800 permanently  they've been dealing with this for years  they've been begging  begging the island's government to fix  this yeah but the tourists that go there  don't know that right  so that's what's so frightening but the  locals will tell you why does it take  tourists to fix what we've been ranting  about for years tourists dying bingo  right and why is the tourism important  because it's the number one the  monastery there yeah i find